# Deno
# https://deno.com/

# Cache directory (when using project-local DENO_DIR)
# https://docs.deno.com/runtime/fundamentals/setup/#deno_dir
.deno/

# The DEPLOYED service's DENO_DIR, which lives inside the deploy dir: the VPS unit
# sets Environment=DENO_DIR=/opt/TNGPlaylists/.deno-cache. The directory must stay
# on disk (the running service reads and writes it), so it is ignored rather than
# removed — that is what keeps `git status --short` in the deploy dir empty, and
# that command is how production state is read (see the vps-deno-app-deployment skill).
.deno-cache/

# Coverage reports
# https://docs.deno.com/runtime/reference/cli/coverage/
coverage/
*.lcov
